# Excalidraw Architecture

## State Management

- Custom state via actionManager — NOT Redux/Zustand/MobX
- State updates: actionManager.executeAction(action, source?, value?) ONLY
- State type: AppState (packages/excalidraw/types.ts)
- Example: `actionManager.executeAction(actionDelete, "ui", selectedIds)`

## Rendering

- Canvas 2D rendering — NOT React DOM for drawing
- Render pipeline: Scene → renderScene() → canvas context
- DO NOT use react-konva, fabric.js, pixi.js

## Dependencies

- No new npm packages without explicit approval
- Check packages/utils/ before adding external helpers

## How to Verify

### State Management

- [ ] Search for Redux/Zustand/MobX imports in changed files
- [ ] Verify all state updates use `actionManager.executeAction()` with proper Action objects
- [ ] Check that custom state conforms to `AppState` type

### Rendering

- [ ] Search for `innerHTML`, `React.render`, or DOM mutation patterns
- [ ] Verify canvas rendering uses canvas context APIs (e.g., `ctx.fillRect()`, `ctx.drawImage()`)
- [ ] Confirm no external canvas libraries imported

### Dependencies

- [ ] Run `yarn audit` to check for new vulnerabilities
- [ ] If modifying `package.json`, verify no new packages added without approval
- [ ] Check `packages/utils/` for existing helpers before writing new utilities
